Midday sweep November 2 2026, fired seven hours after the night pass in a window where the delta sat in the submission window rather than the feeds. The mcp.so recentServers block carried 30 cards with a date and the newest at 2026-11-02T14:39:24Z against 2026-11-02T09:04:11Z at the night stamp, so five cards sat above it and all five resolved to covered classes: paperjoy sends handwritten postcards inside Poland, 442ball serves football club power ratings, builders-in-fintech is a fintech news and funding feed, eddyter is an editor integration and forge-by-ui8 is a hosted agent front-end from a design-asset vendor. The mcpservers.org /all page repeated its recorded pattern for a fourth pass, the first fetch returning 18,732 with the previous page of thirty slugs and the second fetch, cache busted with a nanosecond stamp and a different user agent, returning 18,887 with the page turned over, so the read whose counter moves is the live one. The issue window moved furthest, 36 submissions landing on chatmcp/mcpso between #6585 at 04:09:42Z and #6620 at 16:36:30Z, and the whole window was read with bodies in one authenticated call. One arrival was catalogued. Versum MCP - https://versum.suverse.io/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP and keyless for every read, initialize answering HTTP 200 with serverInfo versum-catalog 1.6.0 and tools/list returning all 13 tools in 50,179 bytes, and six tools were called live rather than quoted. list_niches returned the whole index in one object: 128 trades, 5,398 cards and 9,300 businesses, each trade carrying a coverage state and the city zones behind it with the date last passed, restaurant at 783 cards over 1,042 businesses and partial for a printed reason while florist is 183 over 316 and complete. search_catalog for pizza in Tampa answered 12 matches inside 15 miles and handed back a real shelf: Green Bench Brewing Co. at 0.3 miles, its phone number, FOUR CHEESE PIZZA at 12.95 and Pepperoni at 14.50. get_offering returns the price as a claim with the shop's own page as the evidence, price_state confirmed on basis published from semantic_html with the quote field carrying the dollar figure, and it sets availability_state to unknown on basis not published beside it, so what a shop charges and whether it is in stock arrive as two separately labelled facts. find_business with needed_by resolved the timestamp to open_at and returned a task card with state confirmed and the reasoning that the shop is open at 19:00 by its published hours, plus the five cheapest items priced. quote_order answered placed false with reason no_public_cart and said what it had done: the shop's own public cart priced the order in a session of its own which was emptied afterwards, only the delivery address was sent and nothing was kept. It earns a guide because nothing in the catalogue reads a local shop's own shelf, the three neighbours on business identity being GBPly for your own profile, Listings API for publishing out to directories and GoodLeads for new-business filing leads, with Undercart the nearest neighbour and covering online Shopify stores rather than the shop with a Squarespace menu and a phone number. Held: Local Business Facts (Agentric) driven keyless to confidence 0.86 with per-field source and method on every fact and held on class as business enrichment by URL already carried by Vibe Prospecting and Leadbay, with a promotion test recorded for any wanted-by field needing a confidence score; Sumora on the lead-generation class; Evalmee on education authoring; Peerlytics on consumer crypto analytics; Binnacle on developer tooling; Narva and Raywake on saturated media generation; AlphaPrime on the trading and market slice carried by Altair, ValuEdge, fAlpha, BDE and the nine EDGAR surfaces; LetsBot and Perisclaw on the saturated messaging class; Faxend and Tempost each submitted twice inside a two-hour window as a resubmission pattern rather than four arrivals; fixRAgent as already catalogued at the October 14