Night sweep November 4 2026, five hours after the evening pass. The shape was an undispositioned wave rather than a feed delta. mcpservers.org moved from 19,148 at the evening read to 19,342 here, and 191 of the 201 slugs across /all pages 1 to 7 had no prior disposition under slug, heading, guide directory or spaced product name. The twelve-sitemap canonical put a date on it: 19,305 server URLs now against 19,339 lines in the 22:02 capture, with zero additions and 34 removals, and all 34 are the priority-sitemap slugs (github-mcp-server, slack-mcp-server, notion-mcp-server and siblings) that the server sitemaps never carry. So the wave landed between the evening read and 22:02 and nothing new has entered the sitemaps in the five hours since. The wave decomposed into three cohorts. Fifteen entries across pages 1 and 2 are one repository, foreverworks/mcps, published as separate listings: Google Workspace, Notion, Bitwarden, Porkbun, Home Assistant, Expo EAS, App Store and Google Play reviews, trademark search, TypeSafe, and Romanian financial administration in four pieces (BNR exchange rates, ANAF e-Factura, ANAF SPV, ONRC trade register) plus Oblio invoicing, held on the single-author fleet rule because the four Romanian siblings must be catalogued or held together rather than one picked and because Google Workspace and Notion are first-party connectors most clients already hold. About 25 entries are vendor documentation servers reading -docs-mcp or -docs-mcp-server (Cartrelay, Hirelabs, Ziva.sh, Teddit.io, Echoly, MachineMail, Cloud Alter Ego, La Prueba, Mooi, SimpleVerifier, AskEditor, Mailazy, Robylon, Skael, Buddy, APKCube, IsMyNumberSpam, Back4App, Webclaw, Recl, Rainbrand and siblings), held as a class because a documentation route answers questions about a product rather than about the business. The remainder is vertical utilities and vendor connectors whose classes are already carried: lead generation and creator analytics (Embers, Sumora, Skael, Patto, UGC Chart) with Leadbay, Vibe Prospecting, VOYGR, IQfluence, AffiliateSpy, GenViral and Viral Manager; ads and social publishing (Orphex, Apogee, SyncBooster, Echoly, 24Repost); scraping (Scrappy, Webclaw, MapsScraper) with ScrapeAtlas, Browserless and Crawl4AI; AI visibility (Teddit.io, two pixelcove tools, Krafters) with geolint and LogNorm; site quality (Useful Work, feed 2026-11-04T04:51:22Z, no endpoint on the card) with SiteGoalie and SquirrelScan; CRM and revenue (Deskhand, NOVA for Kommo, Finwise, Reciba, Volanea); property (Homedex UK, BatchData) with Hercules and the property group; and outside scope, Fortrip, shibaSIM, OpenVerein, Neat Icons, Shellway, Lingviko, FateTell, FindBroadband with its outage checker, Kurodyne, PrizePicks, the empty-leg and private-airport indexes, Esta no Ir, ScareMap, Heatwayve, Bodywise, afk-rig and IMPOSSIBREW. Two arrivals were catalogued, both keyless and both driven. ExitValue.ai M&A Multiples MCP at https://exitvalue.ai/api/mcp answered initialize 200 as exitvalue-ai 1.1.0 with all 4 tools listed and 3 called: list_industries returns 15 verticals holding 106 sub-verticals with bracketed ids; get_valuation_multiples on HVAC returned EV/EBITDA median 9.6x with a middle 50% of 8.4x to 14.8x on n=11 and EV/Revenue median 0.95x at 0.60x to 2.20x on n=13 over 14 disclosed transactions at a median deal size of 135 million dollars; compare_industries on dental, HVAC and SaaS returned 11.0x at n=80, 9.6x at n=11 and 14.66x at n=414 with the sample returned as 1,560 transactions and p25, p50, p75 and n mirrored into structuredContent; get_multiples_trend on HVAC returned no years and said why, n below 10 in every single year, and the size-bracket object came back empty while the pooled figure was published and labelled pooled, both isError false with the reason stated; the limits are in the guide, pooled 2018 to 2026 medians hide the cycle, the universe is US disclosed transactions and therefore skewed large, and every response carries a calculator_url with src=mcp that is a marketing funnel separable from the structured data. AllClear Lending MCP at https://fundingos.consultincllc.workers.dev/mcp answered initialize 200 as allclear-lending 0.1.0 with all 8 tools listed and 5 calls made, one rejected against the decline enum: find_lenders for restaurants in Texas returned 12 matches and 4 at the limit, each an institution record with its own source page, Celtic Bank at up to 2 million dollars for restaurant FF&E at up to 100 percent LTV through a referral_partner broker path with confidence sourced, Ready Capital for SBA 7(a) restaurant acquisition cited to a published spotlight deal, and single-source rows labelled unverified in the same field; industry_overview returned ease tier A at 88, NAICS 7225 and 7224, 7 products that fit, SBA eligible, 14 lenders serving and 0 restricting, Toast Capital and Square Loans flagged embedded and not brokerable, a verifier_note carving out nightclubs, and a why field citing 16,354 SBA 7(a) loans to NAICS 722511 over FY20 to FY25 from a third-party FOIA tally; next_best_option enforces its reason as a closed enum of 15 values, a call naming credit was rejected -32602 with the list attached, and the valid low_personal_credit call returned Bitty and Credibly at a 500 to 550 floor with the instruction to show the MCA cost in math and a dated come-back plan ordered cheapest first; two weaknesses are stated rather than smoothed, state_rules for Texas carries dated facts (HB 700 registration with the OCCC through NMLS by 2026-12-31, the SBA Form 159 referral rule, non-citizen ownership ineligible since 2026-03-01) and then returns researched false with every lane unknown, and report_outcome beside lender_stats makes a two-sided graph fed by whoever reports under a self-declared key. The submission window carried 12 items between 6707 at 04:55:34Z and 6718 at 10:02:28Z, and the feed parsed to 28 cards with the newest at 2026-11-04T09:41:03Z and 10 dated after the Integrate.io card the evening pass catalogued. Twelve endpoint probes ran, 4 answering 200 (exitvalue-ai 1.1.0, allclear-lending 0.1.0, dilutionscan-mcp 0.19.0 with 34 tools, shibasim 1.0.0 with 3) and 8 answering 401 (SN Data with OAuth protected-resource metadata, UGC Chart sign_in_required, Fortrip, OpenVerein, 24Repost, Neat Icons, Shellway, txscribe). DilutionScan was held on its own submission, which states tool calls need a DilutionScan Pro subscription, the same subscription behind Signal8 Pro at a vendor already catalogued. Counts: guide tree 1,096 directories before this pass and 1,098 after, 1,240 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,242 after.

Midday sweep November 4 2026, eight hours after the night pass, and the counters moved less than at any point in four passes. The mcp.so homepage was fetched directly with a browser UA and the recentServers block parsed to 124 objects, newest at 2026-11-04T14:37:59Z (Gamebeast), with exactly one card above the night stamp of 2026-11-04T09:41:03Z; the cache-busted read returned zero bytes, the known flap, so the direct read is the one recorded. The mcpservers.org /all newest page was read twice through the reader proxy, returning 19,342 then 19,344, and the difference was composition rather than a cohort: two slugs left the page (the foreverworks EAS entry and reciba) and two entered (lingviko and snapwidget), with every other slug inside the wave the night pass dispositioned by class. The twelve-sitemap canonical settles the window: the 04:30 capture held 19,339 unique server URLs and the 10:15 capture holds 19,344, five additions and zero removals, and the five are astraeye-labs-mcp, exclusive-digits-phone-numbers-mcp, lingviko-com-der-die-das, orinyx-mcp and snapwidget-mcp. The submission window carried 27 items between #6719 at 10:33:39Z and #6745 at 17:27:29Z, read with bodies in one authenticated call; #6745 is a request to retire an unmaintained community prototype in favour of the maintained FinancialFilings server, so the window is 26 arrivals plus one piece of housekeeping. One was catalogued. NMOS.NET Crawl Analytics MCP at https://nmos.net/mcp is cookieless crawler tracking with six read-only tools behind OAuth 2.0 with PKCE, dynamic client registration and a client ID metadata document, and this entry states its tier rather than implying a session because a keyless initialize answered HTTP 401 with JSON-RPC -32001 Unauthorized, so no tool was called. The data arrives by beacon rather than by API: a meta tag plus tracking.js, a no-JS CSS beacon, or a Cloudflare Worker at the edge, with WordPress and GTM on Pro+, and the vendor is explicit that a meta tag alone identifies the site and records no visits. What it answers is the input side of the AI-visibility question this catalogue has only ever measured from the answer side: whether Googlebot reached the important pages with visits, journeys and sitemap gaps, what AI bots are reading as visit trails plus llms.txt coverage match or miss, and which bots hit HTTP errors, robots conflicts or a forged user agent, the last checked by reverse DNS on Pro and above; the vendor's own limit is quoted in the guide, visit records and policy signals rather than search rankings or model-training proof. The pricing line matters: the free plan is 1 site and 100 crawl visits a month with crawl analysis only, and llms.txt coverage, sitemap coverage, bot authenticity and the crawl-like-a-bot simulation all start at Pro at 20 dollars a month, with the integrations panel at Pro+ 40 dollars and yearly billing at ten times monthly. It earns a guide because the answer side is held three ways and the input side none, NM Signals auditing how crawlers would see a URL, AIO.GEO auditing structural readiness and dry-running fixes, and Encited mining Search Console and answer-engine visibility, none of which can say whether the crawler came back after a migration or whether the fetch returned a 403. Held with measurements: Gamebeast from the feed is the official server for one game LiveOps platform and is a single-vendor vertical with a promotion test recorded; workload.zero answered keyless initialize 200 as workload-zero 2.1.0 with 149 tools spanning profile, projects and budgets, clients, tasks, timers, goals, deals, quotes, quote-to-invoice and revenue, the widest surface in the window and a hosted German business suite whose slices are carried by Deskhand, NOVA for Kommo, Finwise, Reciba and Volanea; GameshipKit answered keyless 200 as gameshipkit 1.0.0 with five tools over 69 browser tools for pixel art and store assets and is outside operator scope; Links as a Service answered 401 invalid_token and is a Danish link marketplace with 150k publisher domains at publisher cost plus 20 percent, held because the link-building slice is carried by RankControl and MentionAgent and what remains is a checkout over bought inventory rather than data that is read; Smitline is a self-hosted open-source server for phone calls and Zoom, Teams and Meet attendance, held on two carried classes at once, voice by PlaceCall and meeting notes by Granola, ParrotNotes, Tactiq and Lavox; UX Pilot answered 401 -32001 API key is required and drives UI design on its own canvas; EZ@Work answered 401 and is the freelancer version of the invoicing and time slice. Held on class without a probe because the precedent is settled: astraeye-labs on stock research beside Altair, ValuEdge, fAlpha, BDE and the EDGAR surfaces, exclusive-digits on number inventory, orinyx as a healthcare vertical beside TMSClinics and SleepStudies, lingviko outside scope, snapwidget as a website embed rather than a data surface, Tabula and Kipurse and I Am Wallet and Haris Guardian on agent payments and crypto beside FiatDock, CoinVello, SnapEX Pay and Spectra, Dopamyn on crypto audience intelligence, run.zero on developer PaaS, Mobilebox on device farms, UberLLM and Sirv on media generation, Postly on physical mail, Same Day Website Builder on the site-builder class, CallAI SEO on the twenty-guide SEO class, AI SENSE as an aggregator of 77 free utilities, the three tidybytetools utilities as local developer tools, and seam, Markdown Pipeline, ipvolt and AdminHub for Telegram on diff review, Jira-to-Markdown sync, proxy set-up and hosted Telegram publishing. One execution note is recorded because it will recur: a 10:00 MST attempt on the same surfaces stopped mid-run without committing, so its canonical capture and its /all pages 1 to 5 were reused and the window delta was recomputed as a fresh set difference on the two files rather than read out of the dead run's output. Counts: guide tree 1,098 directories before this pass and 1,099 after, 1,242 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,243 after, mcp.so 124 objects with the newest at 2026-11-04T14:37:59Z, mcpservers.org /all at 19,342 then 19,344, a canonical set difference of five additions and zero removals from 19,339 to 19,344, and six endpoint probes with two answering 200 and four answering 401.
